The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (tag_exists(name))
	n->item = get_item_from_tag(name);
```
Reason:
The logic incorrectly checks for the existence of a tag without considering the special case for the root node. This leads to potential errors when trying to create a node with the name "__root__", as it does not initialize the root node correctly.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (!strcmp(name, "__root__"))
	n->item = list_first_entry_or_null(&menu.master, struct item, master);
else
	n->item = get_item_from_tag(name);
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a specific check for the name "__root__" to initialize the root node differently, ensuring that it retrieves the correct item from the master list instead of relying on the tag existence check, thus preventing the errors associated with the root node creation.

